[38;5;231m⏺[39m I've opened the three layout options in a browser tab so they're easier to compare:
  [94m]8;id=i5wa31;http://localhost:54117/?key=639e11f38261e6024d97128acb09dfeeb847c2d2fdb25a1a6d76915c374c0d28\http://localhost:54117/?key=639e11f38261e6024d97128acb09dfeeb847c2d2fdb25a1a6d76915c374c0d28[39m]8;;\ (this uses a lot of
  tokens, so tell me if you'd rather stay in the terminal).

  [1mCurrent page:[0m [38;5;153mpublic/settings.html[39m has 12 [38;5;153m<label>[39m fields in a single flex column. [38;5;153msettings.js[39m reads the whole form
  with [38;5;153mFormData[39m and POSTs it to [38;5;153m/api/settings[39m. All three options keep that one form and its submit logic as they are.

  [1mProposed groups:[0m
  - [1mProfile:[0m display name, email, avatar URL
  - [1mPreferences:[0m time zone, language, theme
  - [1mNotifications:[0m email, push, weekly digest
  - [1mSecurity:[0m two-factor auth, session timeout, API token

  [1mOptions in the tab:[0m
  - [1mA. Stacked sections:[0m one column with a heading per group. Smallest change: HTML and CSS only.
  - [1mB. Two-column sections:[0m the group title and a short description sit on the left, the fields on the right. It needs a
    wider container and collapses to one column on narrow screens. HTML and CSS only.
  - [1mC. Sidebar tabs:[0m shows one group at a time. It needs tab-switching JS, and it's easy to miss fields on hidden tabs.
    That's probably more than 12 fields need.

  I recommend [1mA[0m. Each group becomes a [38;5;153m<fieldset>[39m with a [38;5;153m<legend>[39m, which is semantic and accessible and doesn't change
  the submitted data. B is a good choice if you expect the page to grow.

  Which layout do you want? You can click one in the browser or reply here. Also tell me if you'd group any fields
  differently.

  Note: the mockups are saved in [38;5;153m.hyperpowers/[39m in the project directory. The repo has no [38;5;153m.gitignore[39m, so you may want to
  add [38;5;153m.hyperpowers/[39m to one.

